{"answer":"No. At n = 40, n^2+n+41 = 1681 = 41^2, which is composite. Thus the statement fails for a nonnegative integer.","approaches":[{"description":"Evaluate the polynomial at a particular nonnegative integer that yields a nontrivial factorization.","id":"counterexample","outcome":"candidate","reason":"The evaluation n=40 produces 41^2, so one counterexample refutes the universal statement."}],"change_log":[],"claims":[{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Arithmetic evaluation and factorization in step-evaluate.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"value-at-forty","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"For n=40, n^2+n+41=1681=41^2.","step_ids":["step-evaluate"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"A square of an integer greater than 1 is composite; applied explicitly in step-composite.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["value-at-forty"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"counterexample-composite","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The value at n=40 is not prime.","step_ids":["step-composite"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"A universal statement over nonnegative integers is refuted by one nonnegative input at which its predicate fails, as applied in step-refute.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["counterexample-composite"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"universal-statement-false","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"It is false that n^2+n+41 is prime for every nonnegative integer n.","step_ids":["step-refute"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":[],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"step-evaluate","justification":"Direct calculation: 40^2+40+41=1600+40+41=1681, and 41^2=1681.","statement":"At n=40, n^2+n+41=41^2."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["step-evaluate"],"id":"step-composite","justification":"Since 41>1, 41^2 has the nontrivial factorization 41·41 and is composite.","statement":"The polynomial value at n=40 is composite."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["step-composite"],"id":"step-refute","justification":"40 is nonnegative, so this composite value is a counterexample to the stated universal assertion.","statement":"The universal primality statement is false."}],"question_status":"refuted","tool_requests":[]}
